  "description": "The package layer under Avig.Kalkyl, Avig.Ord and Avig.Bildspel: reads and writes Open Packaging Conventions files (.xlsx, .docx, .pptx and others), as zip or as Flat OPC, with limits that keep a hostile file from running the process out of memory. Also what the three share: Length, the PresentationML and DrawingML names, and a DrawingML layer that writes and reads shapes, fills, lines, shadows, text, groups, pictures with SVG, and charts of every type (also the newer waterfall, treemap, sunburst, histogram, Pareto, box and whisker, funnel and map charts) with the workbook that keeps their data, whether they sit on a sheet or a slide. Not related to Microsoft's DocumentFormat.OpenXml. No dependencies besides Avig.Result; trimming and Native AOT safe.",
